  abstract = {This article evaluates the implications on transformer model performance in  satellite image classification by means of numerous data augmentation techniques  using the Eurosat dataset. We examine the Swin-tiny, Swin-small, Convit-small, and  Crossvit-small models under several augmentation methods including MixUp,  CutMix, Geometric, WGP-GAN, and DCGAN. Our findings demonstrate that  Mixup and WGP-GAN augmentations significantly enhance model performance;  Swin small achieves 99.26\% test accuracy the best. CutMix was more helpful for  Swin-small than for Swin-tiny; geometric augmentation improved Swin-tiny and  Crossvit-small. DCGAN behaved differently on many models. These results  highlight the significance of selecting appropriate augmentation techniques suited  for certain model architectures to increase performance in assignments needing  satellite image classification.},
